# Auto-fetched 3D assets (use `pnpm fetch:3d`).  We commit the dir layout
# (public/3d/{hdr,cast,props}/) and README but never the binary asset blobs
# themselves — they're CC0 / redownloadable, can be hundreds of MB, and the
# 3D renderer falls back gracefully when files are missing.
public/3d/hdr/*.hdr
public/3d/cast/*.glb
# EXCEPTION: the generated photoreal archetype cast (scripts/make-cast-photoreal.py)
# IS committed — these 14 WebP-textured GLBs (~19 MB total) are the deploy
# artifact that upgrades the live GitHub Pages site from the procedural capsule
# fallback to real MakeHuman humans. Everything else in _lib stays ignored.
public/3d/cast/_lib/*
!public/3d/cast/_lib/*.glb
public/3d/cast/_quaternius/
public/3d/cast/_kenney/
public/3d/cast/_stash_overrides/
# photoreal-cast QA scratch (renders / logs from make-cast-photoreal + render-glb)
scripts/_qa*
scripts/_gen_all.log
public/3d/anims/*.glb
# EXCEPTION: the 7 CC0 Quaternius pose clips ARE committed — without them the
# deployed cast loads but never animates (frozen in bind-pose) and collapsed
# patients stand on the bed instead of lying. Required deploy artifact, like _lib.
!public/3d/anims/*.glb
public/3d/props/*.glb
public/3d/props/_quaternius-medical/
